-- title:
--   Node parameter separates the places above a supersingular place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a level $N\neq 0$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring map $\mathrm{red}:A\to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, and integrality of the two Hecke maps $\overline\alpha,\overline\beta$ from level $N$ to level $Nq$; let $P$ be a place specialisation of these data and $R$ a prolongation tuple over $P$, with $k$ algebraically closed and $q\nmid N$. Assume $R$ is a model (the two divisor laws for the first and second residues together with the two cusp laws) and satisfies `OrderLawFixed`: for $f$ integral for $R_1$ and $R_2$ with both residues nonzero, the push-forward along $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}$ of the divisor of $f$ at an affine geometric place fixed by the square of the geometric Frobenius equals $\mathrm{ord}$ of the first residue plus $\mathrm{ord}$ at the Frobenius translate of the second residue. Let $K\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a number field, and let $w$ be a supersingular place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\;k\;N$ (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set). Assume the value-integrality law at $w$: every $f$ in $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegers}\;w$ has $\mathcal V.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$ for every place $\mathcal V$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,\mathcal V=w$. Let $B=R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\;K\;w$, the subring of elements of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ integral for $R_1$, for $R_2$ and for all places over $w$, whose Laurent expansion lies in the field generated by constants from $K$ and the two $j$-expansions; assume $B$ local and Noetherian, and that every $g\in B$ differs from some constant $o\in A\cap K$ by a non-unit. Let $\varpi\in A\cap K$ generate the kernel of the reduction $A\cap K\to k$. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, $\pi$ irreducible in $W$, $\sigma$ a ring map from $W$ to the $\mathfrak m_B$-adic completion of $B$ sending $\pi$ to the constant $\varpi$, $E\geq 1$, and $\iota$ a ring isomorphism from that completion onto the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$ carrying $\sigma$ to the constants and reading off the branch orders: if the first residue of $f\in B$ is nonzero of order $n$ at $w$ then $\iota(f)$ is a unit multiple of $V^n$ modulo $(\pi,U)$, and if the second residue is nonzero of order $n$ at the Frobenius translate of $w$ then $\iota(f)$ is a unit multiple of $U^n$ modulo $(\pi,V)$. Finally let $c=(x,y)$ be node coordinates over $K$ at $w$ (first residue of $x$ zero, second residue of order $1$ at the Frobenius translate; second residue of $y$ zero, first residue of order $1$ at $w$) with $xy=\varpi^{E_0}u$ for some $E_0$ and some unit $u$ of $B$. Then any two places $\mathcal V,\mathcal V'$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,\mathcal V=P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,\mathcal V'=w$ and $\mathcal V.\mathrm{evalAt}(y)=\mathcal V'.\mathrm{evalAt}(y)$ are equal.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the defining property of the node annulus of $X_0(Nq)$ at a supersingular place: on the branch cut out by the parameter $y$, the value of $y$ determines the place above $w$, the underlying local picture being the crossing equation $xy=\varpi^{E}$ of Deligne–Rapoport. It is used in the existence-and-uniqueness statement for places over $w$ with prescribed $y$-value and in the annulus-domain criterion identifying the places above the node by the parameter.
